---
import DocsLayout from "~/layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---
<DocsLayout active="bench" title="Benchmarks" description="Understand what Redax measures, how the score is produced, and where the published numbers apply.">
  <section><h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">Published result</h2><div class="mt-5 card p-6 sm:p-8"><div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-400">PII200K · mean R-score</div><div class="mt-3 text-[72px] leading-none tracking-[-0.05em] text-ink-0">0.552</div><div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[13px] text-flame-300">GLiNER2 · default detector</div><p class="mt-5 max-w-xl text-[14px] text-ink-300">Measured on a 5,060-document stratified sample. Higher is better; the metric rewards coverage while penalizing sloppy redaction boundaries.</p></div></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">How to read the score</h2><p class="mt-3">RedactionBench combines character-level coverage, strict overlap, and format precision. It is a comparative engineering signal—not a guarantee that every possible entity in every domain will be detected.</p><div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">{[["Recall", "Did we cover the sensitive characters?"], ["Precision", "Did the span boundaries stay tight?"], ["Latency", "How quickly can the boundary respond?"]].map(([title, body]) => <div class="card p-5"><div class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink-0">{title}</div><p class="mt-2 text-[13px] text-ink-400">{body}</p></div>)}</div></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">Reproduce it</h2><p class="mt-3">The benchmark fixtures and runner live in the repository so you can evaluate a policy or detector against the same corpus before shipping.</p><a href="/redax/#deploy" class="btn-ghost mt-6">See deployment options →</a></section>
</DocsLayout>
